@TheEpicDolphin you wrote batch-sharded sampling (#50465). Could you take a look at this fix?

It is still needed on current `main` (4643f4185, 22 Oct): `_dummy_sampler_run` still calls only `compute_logits`, so the sharded `all_to_all_logits` first runs in `warmup_kernels`, after the KV cache is sized. On 8 × A100-40GB with `--enable-batch-sharded-sampling`, start-up then fails with an NCCL out-of-memory (reproducer and memory numbers in the description). The branch is up to date with `main` and merges cleanly; the change is +18 / −1 lines, in the profile path only.

cc @njhill

This condition leaks how `BatchSharder` assigns requests to ranks. `BatchSharder` has all the information it needs to compute the number of locally-owned requests from `idx_mapping_np`. For example:
```
# BatchSharder
def num_local_reqs(self, idx_mapping_np: np.ndarray) -> int:
    if self.draft_logits is None:
        owners = shard_owners(idx_mapping_np.shape[0], self.tp_size)
    else:
        owners, _ = self.draft_logits.owners_of(idx_mapping_np)
    return int(np.count_nonzero(owners == self.tp_rank))
```

Could we use that value instead to determine whether the rank needs the fallback sampler run?

